<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Blue Jacket</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1743–c. 1808</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Weyapiersenwah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Blue Jacket was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shawnee">Shawnee</a> war leader in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ohio">Ohio</a> country. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/little-turtle">Little Turtle</a> of the Miami he led the Western Confederacy of Native nations against American expansion, defeating <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josiah-harmar">Josiah Harmar</a> in 1790 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arthur-st-clair">Arthur St. Clair</a> in 1791. After the defeat at Fallen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timber">Timbers</a> in 1794 he signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-greenville">Treaty of Greenville</a> in 1795, ceding much of Ohio.</p></div>
